dictation-app

This product includes or depends on the following third-party software.

handy-keys 0.3.4 (https://github.com/handy-computer/handy-keys)
  Global keyboard listener behind the macOS hotkey
  (crates/platform/src/hotkey/macos.rs). Vendored with fixes to its macOS
  event tap callback under third_party/handy-keys (changes listed in
  third_party/handy-keys/PATCHES.md; licence in
  third_party/handy-keys/LICENSE).
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 handy-computer

handy-recorder 0.1.0 (https://github.com/handy-computer/handy-recorder)
  Microphone capture behind the macOS audio adapter
  (crates/platform/src/audio/macos.rs): the CoreAudio callback, lock-free
  ring buffer, mono mix and resampling to 16 kHz. Used as a dependency; no
  code copied. Its own dependencies include handy-cpal 0.18.2
  (Apache-2.0), rubato 5.0.0 and rtrb 0.4.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 handy-computer

coreaudio-rs 0.14.2 (https://github.com/RustAudio/coreaudio-rs)
  The CoreAudio wrapper under handy-cpal. Vendored with a patch to its
  input callback buffer in third_party/coreaudio-rs (PATCHES.md there),
  with its licence files.
  MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2015 the coreaudio-rs authors
  (mitchmindtree, yupferris and contributors).

handy-cpal 0.18.2, rubato 5.0.0
  Also used directly by the macOS audio adapter: handy-cpal to read the
  current default input, rubato to compute handy-recorder's resampler
  delay. Used as dependencies; no code copied. Apache-2.0 (handy-cpal),
  MIT OR Apache-2.0 (rubato).

objc2, block2, objc2-av-foundation (https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2)
  The macOS microphone permission check and prompt
  (crates/platform/src/permissions/macos.rs). Used as dependencies.
  MIT License (objc2, block2); objc2-av-foundation under
  Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT.

Ideas only, no code: Handy (MIT) for keeping the microphone open briefly
between dictations; Muesli (MIT) for never waiting on CoreAudio from the
thread that drives the UI and for treating route changes as a reason to
reopen the device.

Handy (https://github.com/cjpais/Handy), src-tauri/src/input.rs at commit
9e57a0d
  Adapted: the Carbon/CoreFoundation declarations and the UCKeyTranslate
  scan that finds the key typing "v" with Command in the current keyboard
  layout (crates/platform/src/insert/macos.rs, module `layout`).
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 CJ Pais

objc2-app-kit, objc2-foundation, objc2-core-graphics
(https://github.com/madsmtm/objc2)
  NSPasteboard access and the paste key events
  (crates/platform/src/insert/macos.rs). Used as dependencies.
  Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT.

Ideas only, no code: Muesli (MIT), PasteShortcut.swift, for resolving the
paste key from the layout at paste time with Command held.

keyring 3.6.3 (https://github.com/hwchen/keyring-rs)
  The macOS keychain behind the API-key store
  (crates/platform/src/secrets.rs). Used as a dependency; no code copied.
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.

tauri-specta 2.0.0-rc.26, specta 2.0.0-rc.26, specta-typescript 0.0.13
(https://github.com/specta-rs)
  Typed Tauri commands and the generated src/bindings.ts
  (src-tauri/src/commands.rs). Used as dependencies. MIT License. Their
  build-time proc-macros pull in Inflector 0.11.4 (BSD-2-Clause) and paste
  1.0.15 (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

@tauri-apps/api 2 (https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri)
  The invoke function the generated bindings call. Apache-2.0 OR MIT.

